    "**What this cell does:**  \n",
    "Loads two things from the model files: the **tokenizer** (converts your English text into numbers the AI understands) and the **model itself** (the actual intelligence that generates responses).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why `bfloat16`?** By default, AI models store their numbers in full 32-bit precision — very accurate but very memory-hungry. `bfloat16` cuts that in half with almost no loss in quality. Think of it like compressing a photo from RAW to JPEG — still looks great, takes half the space.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why `device_map=\"auto\"`?** This tells Transformers to automatically figure out how to spread the model across available hardware (GPU + CPU if needed). You don't have to manually manage any of that."
